Shell keys (vi insert and normal mode)
--------------------------------------
- `ctrl-t`   : Paste selected files/dirs (fd, with bat preview)
- `ctrl-r`   : Search history (`?` toggles preview of long commands)
- `alt-c`    : cd into selected directory (Left Option is Alt in WezTerm)
- `**<Tab>`  : Fuzzy completion, e.g. `vim **<Tab>`, `cd **<Tab>`

Inside fzf (FZF_DEFAULT_OPTS, also fzf.vim)
-------------------------------------------
- `tab` / `shift-tab` : Mark / unmark (multi-select is on)
- `ctrl-a`   : Select all and accept
- `F2`       : Toggle preview (hidden by default)
- `F3`       : Open item in bat (or less)
- `ctrl-d` / `ctrl-u` : Half page down / up
- `ctrl-y`   : Copy selection to clipboard (macOS only)

Defaults
--------
- One match is accepted at once (`-1`). File list is `git ls-files` in a repo, else `fd`.
